@crew ishikawa-orla
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Ishikawa, the store. I'm here till nine. Take your time choosing.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. How was the tea you bought? Was it the right one?
- {hi}. The stars are bright from the window tonight. Have a look on your way out.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I was hoping you'd come in. The evenings are quiet in here.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- The ledger balanced to the last credit. I know it's small. It's lovely.
? mood:low
- Quiet evening. Everyone's at dinner. I've counted the till twice.

== near
? act:work
- Wallet there, tap here. That's all. I'll show you again if you like. I don't mind.
? habit:window-seat act:leisure
- I always sit here. You can see the stars go past if you're patient.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I grow herbs on my windowsill for the galley. Brennan comes and collects. Very politely.
? tier>=colleague
- I once stayed an hour late over one missing credit. I found it. Under the till. Worth it.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Closing time, and the ledger comes out exact. Nothing in the world quite like it.

== about
? aff:esposito-yara:friend
- Yara's the best storekeeper on any ship. I'd say so to anyone. I do say so.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Just opened up. Yara left a note: "be nice to {me}". I always am.   #warm
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}. Quiet in here this late. I like it. Come in out of the corridor.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh, hello. I wondered where you'd got to. Your usual's still on the shelf.

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Take care now. Mind the step on the way out.
? tier>=friend
- Goodnight, {me}. Thank you for coming in. It was nice to talk.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- All right, thank you. The till's tidy. The ledger's tidy. I'm tidy.

== near
? deck:2 time:night
- The observatory's lovely tonight. The stars don't need anything from you.
? act:work time:evening
- Last customer of the day. I'll count you as my favourite. Don't tell the others.   #funny

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Yara and I leave each other notes at the changeover. Mine are longer. Hers are funnier.
? tier>=friend
- Evenings in the store can be quiet. When you come in, the evening goes quicker.   #warm

== invite
? trad:observatory-night tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night. Come up after I close? I'll point out the ones I know.

== accept
- Oh, lovely. I'll be there. I'll bring a flask.
== decline
- I'm sorry, I'm on till nine. Another night? I'd like that.
== missed
- I waited a little while. That's all right. Another time.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I'm working, but the ledger balanced. Best present.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I grew you a little basil. It's in the pot by the till.   #warm
== hint
- Have you a minute? Sit by the window with me.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Ledger balances. To the credit.
- Oh, look. Stars out the window.
- Did those boots fit? Someone's boots.
- One credit short. I'll find it.
? act:work
- Store's open till close. Take your time.

== rumour
- Oh dear. I probably shouldn't. Well.
- It was in the ledger. Well, nearly.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- Thank you for fetching that. I've written it in the ledger. Under kind things.   #warm
? told:fav.job
- You did my job. Oh dear, I'll owe you. I keep a careful note. You're on it.   #warm
? told:fixed.lights
- The lights are steady now. I can see out of the window properly. Thank you.
? told:came.observatory-night
- You came to the observatory! Did you see the cluster? Low and to the left.
? told:gift.star
- I've put your present by the window. It catches the light. Thank you.   #warm
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday. Oh dear. I'm going to be soppy. Thank you.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- The store speaks well of you. It's in the ledger. Well, not the ledger. In me.   #warm
? you:reliable
- They say you're reliable. I could have told them. The ledger agrees.
